<p><strong>A source-linked evidence corpus, work in progress.</strong> Figures are as published by
the companies, not audits. Where a figure could not be confirmed, the row says so.</p>

<p>Every row on this site is a public fact: a provider's own page, a vendor's own exam guide,
a filing, a press release. Each one carries a source link and a date it was last checked — see
<a href="/sources/">how this is compiled</a>. Prices, capacities and specs published by a
company about itself are that company's own claim, not an independent audit. Found something
wrong, missing or out of date? <a href="/corrections/">Send a correction</a>.</p>

<p>New to this? Start with <a href="/what-is-a-neocloud/">what a neocloud is, and how to check one</a>.</p>

<div class="map">
{% set cardCopy = {
  "Providers": "Neoclouds, marketplaces, inference platforms and the landlords behind them.",
  "Paths": "Ordered learning paths: fabric, ops, rack, facility, cooling.",
  "Exams": "Vendor exams worth sitting, and the ones to skip.",
  "Courses": "Vendor courses, mapped against the exams they prepare you for.",
  "Cooling": "CDU and TCS/FWS loops, dry coolers, and the rest of the cooling stack.",
  "Vocabulary": "Terms from SUNK to GPUDirect Storage, each sourced.",
  "Events": "Dated, sourced developments in neocloud land.",
  "Leasing": "What a landlord expects before it signs with an AI tenant."
} %}
{% set cardCount = {
  "Providers": site.providers.length,
  "Paths": site.paths.length,
  "Exams": site.exams.length,
  "Courses": site["vendor-courses"].length,
  "Cooling": site["cooling-topics"].length,
  "Vocabulary": site.vocabulary.length,
  "Events": site.events.length,
  "Leasing": site.leasing.length
} %}
{% for n in meta.nav %}
{% if n.label != "About" and n.label != "Start here" %}
  <a href="{{ n.url }}">
    <h2>{{ n.label }}</h2>
    <p class="meta">{{ cardCount[n.label] }} &middot; {{ cardCopy[n.label] }}</p>
  </a>
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
</div>

<section id="recent">
  <h2>Recently confirmed</h2>
  <ul class="recent">
  {% for r in site.providers | recentlyChecked(5) %}
    <li><a href="/providers/{{ r.id }}/">{{ r.name }}</a> &middot; last confirmed {{ r.checked | isoDate }}</li>
  {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<div>
  <p>Steps, exams and courses carry a verdict:</p>
  <ul class="legend">
    <li><span class="chip core">Core</span> do this</li>
    <li><span class="chip opt">Optional</span> useful, not required</li>
    <li><span class="chip later">Later</span> worth it eventually</li>
    <li><span class="chip skip">Skip</span> not worth the time</li>
  </ul>
</div>
